1
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:21,530
You're wearing a black cloak again.

2
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:24,220
I've been sent to negotiate with you.

3
00:03:53,550 --> 00:03:56,310
It appears my trusting nature got the better of me.

4
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:58,130
It's happened before.

5
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:00,090
I was hoping your loyalty was real

6
00:04:00,090 --> 00:04:02,020
when you pledged yourself to us, Jon Snow.

7
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:03,520
Truly I was.

8
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:05,630
The Halfhand ordered me to join your army

9
00:04:05,630 --> 00:04:08,440
and bring back whatever information I could to Castle Black.

10
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:10,740
He made me kill him so you'd trust me.

11
00:04:10,930 --> 00:04:12,470
I was loyal,

12
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:15,510
to him and to my Night's Watch vows.

13
00:04:15,510 --> 00:04:17,210
All your vows?

14
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,700
She wasn't enough to turn you, eh?

15
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,930
Were you enough to turn her?

16
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:29,230
She put three arrows in me when I escaped.

17
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,910
Did you see her again at Castle Black?

18
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:36,510
-Yes.  -And?

19
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:39,080
She's dead.

20
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:43,040
-Your doing?  -No.

21
00:04:45,590 --> 00:04:47,080
We'll drink to her.

22
00:05:10,610 --> 00:05:12,680
Of all the ways I'd kill you,

23
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,810
poison would be the last.

24
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,410
-Ygritte.  -Ygritte.

25
00:05:29,970 --> 00:05:31,030
That's not wine.

26
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:34,240
No, it's a proper northern drink, Jon Snow.

27
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:37,500
You did well. Fought hard.

28
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,580
Killed some of our strongest men.

29
00:05:40,150 --> 00:05:42,270
One of our giants went into your tunnel

30
00:05:42,270 --> 00:05:44,120
and never came out again.

31
00:05:44,830 --> 00:05:46,480
Mag the Mighty.

32
00:05:46,770 --> 00:05:48,190
He's dead.

33
00:05:48,930 --> 00:05:50,640
He killed my friend Grenn.

34
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,230
He was their king.

35
00:05:52,230 --> 00:05:54,590
The last of a bloodline that stretches back

36
00:05:54,590 --> 00:05:56,440
before the First Men.

37
00:05:56,550 --> 00:05:58,460
Grenn came from a farm.

38
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:06,090
-Mag and Grenn.  -Grenn and Mag.

39
00:06:08,370 --> 00:06:11,370
Kullback, could I trouble you for something to eat?

40
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:15,830
I don't imagine our guest has eaten anything for quite some time.

41
00:06:17,260 --> 00:06:21,420
So, you're here to strike a bargain?

42
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:24,940
Turn your army around and go home.

43
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:27,240
You know I know you're low on arrows,

44
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,360
you're low on oil, you're low on men.

45
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:31,660
How many are left, 50?

46
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,410
I told Tormund and Orell.

47
00:06:33,530 --> 00:06:35,210
We have more than 1,000 men.

48
00:06:35,210 --> 00:06:36,680
I showed you everything I had.

49
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,830
The whole army, 100,000 strong.

50
00:06:38,830 --> 00:06:42,140
And what did you do? You fired on us with everything you had.

51
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:43,220
It wasn't much.

52
00:06:43,530 --> 00:06:44,770
As soon as I saw that,

53
00:06:44,770 --> 00:06:48,110
I sent 400 men to climb the Wall,

54
00:06:48,110 --> 00:06:50,720
an unmanned stretch five miles west of here.

55
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:52,390
A lot of them will die climbing,

56
00:06:52,390 --> 00:06:54,910
but most of them will be over by the end of the day.

57
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:57,810
It's me being honest with you, Jon Snow,

58
00:06:57,820 --> 00:07:00,090
which is more than you've ever done for me.

59
00:07:00,090 --> 00:07:02,350
My people have bled enough.

60
00:07:02,710 --> 00:07:04,110
We're not here to conquer.

61
00:07:04,110 --> 00:07:06,880
We're here to hide behind your Wall.

62
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:11,200
Just like you. We need your tunnel.

63
00:07:11,570 --> 00:07:14,860
Now we both know that winter is coming.

64
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:18,200
And if my people aren't south of the Wall when it comes in earnest,

65
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:20,390
we'll all end up worse than dead.

66
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:23,150
You want to strike a bargain with me?

67
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:24,610
Here's the bargain.

68
00:07:24,710 --> 00:07:26,990
You go back, you open the gates to us,

69
00:07:26,990 --> 00:07:30,210
and I swear to you that no one else will die.

70
00:07:30,430 --> 00:07:32,140
Refuse,

71
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:35,600
and we'll kill every last man at Castle Black.

72
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:46,360
Oh, that's why you're here.

73
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:49,620
I reckon you could do it before any of them could stop you.

74
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:51,390
They'd kill you, of course.

75
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,900
They'd kill you slow.

76
00:07:52,910 --> 00:07:56,210
But you knew that when you came in here.

77
00:07:57,040 --> 00:08:00,850
Are you capable of that, Jon Snow?

78
00:08:00,850 --> 00:08:04,180
Killing a man in his own tent when he's just offered you peace?

79
00:08:04,270 --> 00:08:06,650
Is that what the Night's Watch is?

80
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,700
Is that what you are?

81
00:08:11,790 --> 00:08:13,220
Riders coming!

82
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:16,500
-Are you attacking us?  -No.

83
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:18,270
It's like you said, we don't have the men.

84
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:49,040
Hold! To me! To me!

85
00:10:00,930 --> 00:10:02,360
Stand down!

86
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:06,900
I said my people have bled enough

87
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:08,780
and I meant it.

88
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:44,680
Round them up.

89
00:10:56,750 --> 00:10:58,770
You're the King-beyond-the-Wall?

90
00:11:01,570 --> 00:11:04,040
-Do you know who I am?  -Never had the pleasure.

91
00:11:04,050 --> 00:11:05,290
This is Stannis Baratheon,

92
00:11:05,290 --> 00:11:07,310
the one true king of the Seven Kingdoms.

93
00:11:07,310 --> 00:11:08,820
We're not in the Seven Kingdoms

94
00:11:08,820 --> 00:11:10,600
and you're not dressed for this weather.

95
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:15,180
It is customary to kneel when surrendering to a king.

96
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:23,120
We do not kneel.

97
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:25,640
I'll have thousands of your men in chains by nightfall,

98
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:27,880
have nowhere to put them, have nothing to feed them.

99
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,810
I'm not here to slaughter beat dogs.

100
00:11:30,810 --> 00:11:33,380
Their fate depends on their king.

101
00:11:34,530 --> 00:11:38,320
All the same, we do not kneel.

102
00:11:40,890 --> 00:11:42,610
Take these men away.

103
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:46,690
What's a man of the Night's Watch doing in a wildling camp?

104
00:11:48,190 --> 00:11:50,940
I was sent to discuss terms with the King-beyond-the-Wall.

105
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:53,010
You're speaking to the one true king, boy.

106
00:11:53,410 --> 00:11:55,190
You will address him as Your Grace.

107
00:11:55,190 --> 00:11:58,670
I know he's the king. My father died for him.

108
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:02,840
My name is Jon Snow, Your Grace.

109
00:12:04,070 --> 00:12:05,770
I'm Ned Stark's son.

110
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:10,640
Your father was an honorable man.

111
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,240
He was, Your Grace.

112
00:12:12,550 --> 00:12:14,640
What do you think he'd have done with him?

113
00:12:20,770 --> 00:12:22,800
I was this man's prisoner once.

114
00:12:23,450 --> 00:12:25,940
He could have tortured me. He could have killed me.

115
00:12:27,710 --> 00:12:29,350
But he spared my life.

116
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:31,860
I think my father would have taken him prisoner,

117
00:12:31,910 --> 00:12:33,590
listened to what he had to say.

118
00:12:37,270 --> 00:12:39,850
Very well, then. Take him.

119
00:12:46,250 --> 00:12:47,500
Your Grace.

120
00:12:48,410 --> 00:12:51,070
If my father had seen the things that I've seen,

121
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:54,040
he'd also tell you to burn the dead before nightfall.

122
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:57,170
All of them.

123
00:13:06,170 --> 00:13:08,680
I would suggest milk of the poppy

124
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:11,350
to ease his pain, but he is completely insensate.

125
00:13:11,350 --> 00:13:12,610
Bloody Martells.

126
00:13:12,610 --> 00:13:14,910
The cause appears to be manticore venom.

127
00:13:14,910 --> 00:13:17,540
It is. The Death's Head manticore.

128
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:21,100
Yes, I've read a great deal about it.

129
00:13:21,110 --> 00:13:22,640
It's a horrible poison.

130
00:13:22,850 --> 00:13:25,280
Usually Mantari in origin.

131
00:13:26,510 --> 00:13:27,800
Yes, yes.

132
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,040
There's nothing to be done.

133
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:30,520
Yes, there is.

134
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:34,770
May I ask what you think you're doing?

135
00:13:34,770 --> 00:13:35,920
Saving him.

136
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:38,080
Your Grace, I wish it were otherwise,

137
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:41,030
but Ser Gregor is beyond saving.

138
00:13:41,030 --> 00:13:42,850
Well, well beyond.

139
00:13:42,850 --> 00:13:45,360
This man is not even a maester,

140
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:47,690
let alone Grand Maester.

141
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:49,140
That's for the best.

142
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:51,180
No maester knows how to save him.

143
00:13:51,180 --> 00:13:53,090
That is exactly the sort of arrogance

144
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:55,980
that had him expelled from the Citadel, Your Grace.

145
00:13:55,980 --> 00:14:00,100
His curiosity was deemed dangerous and unnatural.

146
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:02,330
Rightly so, in my opinion.

147
00:14:02,370 --> 00:14:04,610
You're dismissed, Grand Maester.

148
00:14:06,150 --> 00:14:10,480
But, Your Grace, this is my laboratory.

149
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:12,980
-Not anymore.  -But I.

150
00:14:20,070 --> 00:14:22,990
-You can save him?  -Difficult to say, Your Grace.

151
00:14:22,990 --> 00:14:25,560
But if my past work is any guide,

152
00:14:27,770 --> 00:14:29,320
we stand a chance.

153
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:31,490
Do everything you can.

154
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,160
Come to me for anything you need.

155
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,630
Thank you, Your Grace.

156
00:14:35,150 --> 00:14:36,520
You should know,

157
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:39,830
the process may change him,

158
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:42,130
somewhat.

159
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:46,950
Will it weaken him?

160
00:14:48,150 --> 00:14:49,380
Oh, no.

161
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:51,650
Very well, then.

162
00:15:10,770 --> 00:15:12,340
Not another word.

163
00:15:12,530 --> 00:15:14,990
We've been over this. The matter's closed.

164
00:15:14,990 --> 00:15:16,630
I'm opening it again.

165
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:21,070
You were betrothed to Loras Tyrell.

166
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:23,470
You're still betrothed to Loras Tyrell.

167
00:15:23,470 --> 00:15:25,750
And you will marry Loras Tyrell

168
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:28,090
as soon as Tommen marries Margaery.

169
00:15:28,090 --> 00:15:29,420
I will not.

170
00:15:29,670 --> 00:15:32,420
Jaime cannot marry or inherit lands.

171
00:15:32,420 --> 00:15:35,480
Tyrion's sentence will be carried out tomorrow.

172
00:15:37,810 --> 00:15:41,020
You have on several occasions made great claims

173
00:15:41,030 --> 00:15:43,680
about your commitment to this family's future.

174
00:15:43,690 --> 00:15:45,190
Your role in that future

175
00:15:45,190 --> 00:15:47,760
is more vital now than it ever was.

176
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:48,950
I don't care.

177
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,550
I will stay in King's Landing

178
00:15:50,550 --> 00:15:52,960
where I belong with my son the king.

179
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:56,270
When you were nine years old, I was called to the capital.

180
00:15:56,270 --> 00:15:59,340
I decided to take your brother with me and not you.

181
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:02,470
You insisted that you would not be left at Casterly Rock

182
00:16:02,470 --> 00:16:05,140
under any circumstances. And if you recall.

183
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:07,410
I'm not interested in hearing another one of your smug stories

184
00:16:07,410 --> 00:16:09,410
about the time you won.

185
00:16:09,430 --> 00:16:11,850
This isn't going to be one of those times.

186
00:16:11,950 --> 00:16:13,700
Do you think you'll be the first person

187
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:16,580
dragged into a sept to be married against her will?

188
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:18,690
When you marched into the throne room to tell me

189
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:21,520
we'd won the Battle of Blackwater, do you remember?

190
00:16:23,530 --> 00:16:25,860
I was sitting on the Iron Throne with Tommen.

191
00:16:26,430 --> 00:16:28,210
I was about to give him essence of nightshade.

192
00:16:28,210 --> 00:16:30,160
That's how far I was willing to go when I thought

193
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:33,280
someone awful had come to take my son away.

194
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:37,560
Someone awful is coming to take him away.

195
00:16:37,590 --> 00:16:39,950
-No.  -Joffrey is dead.

196
00:16:39,950 --> 00:16:41,910
Myrcella's been sold like livestock.

197
00:16:41,910 --> 00:16:44,910
And now you want to ship me off to Highgarden and steal my boy.

198
00:16:44,910 --> 00:16:46,430
My last boy.

199
00:16:47,830 --> 00:16:49,510
Margaery will dig her claws in,

200
00:16:49,510 --> 00:16:51,780
you will dig your claws in and you'll fight over him,

201
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:54,270
like beasts until you rip him apart.

202
00:16:54,270 --> 00:16:58,080
I will burn our house to the ground before I let that happen.

203
00:16:58,140 --> 00:17:00,090
And how will you do that?

204
00:17:02,430 --> 00:17:03,830
I'll tell everyone the truth.

205
00:17:03,930 --> 00:17:05,970
What truth would that be?

206
00:17:11,010 --> 00:17:12,360
You don't know, do you?

207
00:17:14,670 --> 00:17:15,980
You never believed it.

208
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:19,290
How is that possible?

209
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:23,870
What am I saying? Of course it's possible.

210
00:17:24,330 --> 00:17:27,860
How can someone so consumed by the idea of his family

211
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:30,730
have any conception what his actual family was doing?

212
00:17:32,350 --> 00:17:34,850
We were right there in front of you and you didn't see us.

213
00:17:35,290 --> 00:17:37,390
One look in the past 20 years,

214
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:40,650
one real look at your own children and you would have known.

215
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:42,540
Known what?

216
00:17:43,890 --> 00:17:45,390
Everything they say is true.

217
00:17:45,390 --> 00:17:46,900
-About Jaime and me.  -No.

218
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:49,470
-Your legacy is a lie.  -No, no, no, no.

219
00:17:49,930 --> 00:17:51,210
I don't believe you.

220
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:57,300
Yes, you do.

221
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:16,200
Jaime.

222
00:18:18,630 --> 00:18:19,610
You won.

223
00:18:19,770 --> 00:18:22,810
One fewer brother. Must be proud of yourself.

224
00:18:23,250 --> 00:18:25,120
There's really nothing you wouldn't do, is there?

225
00:18:25,130 --> 00:18:26,990
For my family, no, nothing.

226
00:18:26,990 --> 00:18:29,070
I would do things for my family you couldn't imagine.

227
00:18:29,070 --> 00:18:31,830
-Tyrion is your family.  -He's not.

228
00:18:31,830 --> 00:18:34,830
-You don't get to choose.  -I do. So do you.

229
00:18:35,090 --> 00:18:36,090
You can choose the creature

230
00:18:36,090 --> 00:18:38,170
that killed our mother to come into this world.

231
00:18:38,170 --> 00:18:40,550
Are you really mad enough to blame him for that?

232
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:43,160
He didn't decide to kill her. He was an infant.

233
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:45,080
A disease doesn't decide to kill you.

234
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:47,400
All the same, you cut it out before it does.

235
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:51,110
What do you decide? What do you choose?

236
00:18:51,110 --> 00:18:52,600
The things I did to get back to you,

237
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:55,490
to endure all that, only to find you.

238
00:18:58,500 --> 00:18:59,860
I choose you.

239
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:02,170
-Those are words.  -Yes.

240
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,370
Like the ones I just said to Father.

241
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:06,970
I told him.

242
00:19:07,940 --> 00:19:08,750
Told him what?

243
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:10,500
I told him about us.

244
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:13,530
You told him?

245
00:19:13,530 --> 00:19:15,700
I told him, I won't marry Loras Tyrell.

246
00:19:15,710 --> 00:19:19,640
I told him I'm staying right here with Tommen, with you.

247
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:20,820
You think he'll just accept that?

248
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:22,120
Go and ask him.

249
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:26,900
What did you say?

250
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:29,600
I don't want to talk about Tywin Lannister.

251
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:31,870
I don't choose Tywin Lannister.

252
00:19:31,870 --> 00:19:33,470
I don't love Tywin Lannister.

253
00:19:33,470 --> 00:19:35,720
I love my brother.

254
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:37,870
I love my lover.

255
00:19:39,100 --> 00:19:41,100
People will whisper, they'll make their jokes.

256
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:42,020
Let them.

257
00:19:42,740 --> 00:19:45,050
They're all so small, I can't even see them.

258
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,540
I only see what matters.

259
00:19:56,850 --> 00:19:57,920
Someone will walk in.

260
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,070
I don't care.

261
00:20:36,170 --> 00:20:39,240
I can speak the common tongue if you wish.

262
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,850
You speak it very well.

263
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:44,820
Before you freed me, I belonged to Master Mighdal.

264
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:46,510
I was tutor to his children.

265
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:49,430
I taught them languages and history.

266
00:20:49,830 --> 00:20:53,270
They know a great deal about your family because of me.

267
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:55,880
Little Calla is only seven,

268
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:58,450
but she admires you very much.

269
00:20:58,450 --> 00:21:01,630
I hope I can prove worthy of her admiration.

270
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:03,460
What can I do for you?

271
00:21:05,110 --> 00:21:07,770
When you took the city, the children begged me

272
00:21:07,770 --> 00:21:09,690
not to leave the house.

273
00:21:10,410 --> 00:21:14,050
But Master Mighdal and I agreed that I must.

274
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:16,490
So I lost my home.

275
00:21:18,350 --> 00:21:20,810
Now I live on the streets.

276
00:21:20,810 --> 00:21:22,490
I have outfitted mess halls

277
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:23,930
to feed all former slaves

278
00:21:23,930 --> 00:21:24,840
and barracks to shelter them.

279
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:27,730
I do not mean to offend, Your Grace.

280
00:21:27,730 --> 00:21:30,270
I went to one of these places.

281
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:33,150
The young prey on the old.

282
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:34,170
Take what they want

283
00:21:34,170 --> 00:21:35,940
and beat us if we resist.

284
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:38,800
My Unsullied will make them safe again in short order,

285
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,610
my friend, this I promise you.

286
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:44,520
Even if they are safe, who would I be there?

287
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:47,470
What purpose would I serve?

288
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:50,650
With my master, I was a teacher.

289
00:21:50,650 --> 00:21:54,100
I had the respect and love of his children.

290
00:21:54,560 --> 00:21:56,700
What is it that you want from me?

291
00:21:56,710 --> 00:21:59,350
Your Grace, I ask you

292
00:21:59,350 --> 00:22:02,560
to let me sell myself back to Master Mighdal.

293
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:05,350
You want to return to a man who owned you

294
00:22:05,350 --> 00:22:07,370
like a goat or a chair?

295
00:22:07,370 --> 00:22:09,010
Please, Your Grace.

296
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:12,610
The young may rejoice in the new world you have built for them,

297
00:22:12,620 --> 00:22:15,650
but for those of us too old to change,

298
00:22:15,650 --> 00:22:19,720
there is only fear and squalor.

299
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:22,070
I am not alone.

300
00:22:22,790 --> 00:22:25,870
There are many outside waiting to beg the same of you.

301
00:22:25,870 --> 00:22:27,360
I did not take this city

302
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:30,700
to preside over the injustice I fought to destroy.

303
00:22:30,700 --> 00:22:33,130
I took it to bring people freedom.

304
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:38,000
But freedom means making your own choices.

305
00:22:38,580 --> 00:22:41,800
I will allow you to sign a contract with your former master.

306
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:45,320
It may not cover a period lasting longer than a year.

307
00:22:45,320 --> 00:22:47,090
Thank you, Your Grace.

308
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:50,140
Thank you.

309
00:22:56,060 --> 00:22:58,650
The masters will take advantage of this situation.

310
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:02,140
The men serving them

311
00:23:02,460 --> 00:23:04,710
will be slaves in all, but name.

312
00:23:11,910 --> 00:23:13,610
Approach, my friend.

313
00:23:38,100 --> 00:23:39,770
I have brought you.

314
00:23:44,610 --> 00:23:46,380
He came from the sky.

315
00:23:48,420 --> 00:23:49,430
The black one.

316
00:23:54,530 --> 00:23:55,980
The winged shadow.

317
00:23:57,510 --> 00:23:59,330
He came from the sky and.

318
00:24:04,940 --> 00:24:05,850
My girl.

319
00:24:07,850 --> 00:24:09,190
My little girl.

320
00:24:14,020 --> 00:24:15,220
What was her name?

321
00:24:15,660 --> 00:24:17,170
Zala, Your Grace.

322
00:24:17,170 --> 00:24:20,200
-How old was she?  -Three.

323
00:24:21,590 --> 00:24:22,430
Three.

324
00:27:11,110 --> 00:27:12,450
They came to us

325
00:27:12,450 --> 00:27:15,310
from White Harbor and Barrowton,

326
00:27:15,510 --> 00:27:18,880
from Fairmarket and King's Landing,

327
00:27:19,640 --> 00:27:21,570
from north and south,

328
00:27:21,570 --> 00:27:23,580
from east and west.

329
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:29,170
They died protecting men, women, and children,

330
00:27:29,170 --> 00:27:31,510
who will never know their names.

331
00:27:31,730 --> 00:27:34,390
It is for us to remember them.

332
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:35,960
Our brothers,

333
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:39,260
we shall never see their like again.

334
00:27:39,260 --> 00:27:41,670
And now their watch is ended.

335
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:47,030
And now their watch is ended.

336
00:28:58,650 --> 00:29:01,420
Your old blind man patched me up.

337
00:29:01,890 --> 00:29:02,620
Why?

338
00:29:02,620 --> 00:29:05,880
He's sworn to treat all wounded men, friend or foe.

339
00:29:05,890 --> 00:29:08,400
You want me alive, so you can torture me?

340
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:09,760
No one's gonna torture you.

341
00:29:09,760 --> 00:29:13,440
So how do we die? Hanging? Beheading?

342
00:29:14,100 --> 00:29:15,630
Drop us from the top of the Wall?

343
00:29:15,630 --> 00:29:17,580
I don't know what happens to the prisoners.

344
00:29:18,370 --> 00:29:19,480
Who decides?

345
00:29:20,190 --> 00:29:21,960
I suppose Stannis does.

346
00:29:23,090 --> 00:29:24,680
He your king now?

347
00:29:25,350 --> 00:29:26,570
I don't have a king.

348
00:29:28,260 --> 00:29:31,270
You spent too much time with us, Jon Snow.

349
00:29:32,700 --> 00:29:35,200
You can never be a kneeler again.

350
00:29:35,520 --> 00:29:37,660
We're gonna burn the bodies of your dead.

351
00:29:39,500 --> 00:29:41,260
Do you want to say any words over them?

352
00:29:41,260 --> 00:29:43,820
Words? What kind of words?

353
00:29:43,820 --> 00:29:47,070
Funeral words. I don't know how the free folk do it.

354
00:29:47,070 --> 00:29:47,950
Do what?

355
00:29:49,160 --> 00:29:50,470
Say farewell.

356
00:29:51,770 --> 00:29:53,900
The dead can't hear us, boy.

357
00:29:59,660 --> 00:30:00,500
Snow.

358
00:30:05,380 --> 00:30:06,500
Did you love her?

359
00:30:09,940 --> 00:30:11,250
She loved you.

360
00:30:12,900 --> 00:30:13,900
She told you?

361
00:30:14,380 --> 00:30:15,190
No.

362
00:30:15,760 --> 00:30:17,960
All she ever talked about was killing you.

363
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:20,240
That's how I know.

364
00:30:23,480 --> 00:30:25,460
She belongs in the North.

365
00:30:26,800 --> 00:30:28,320
The real North.

366
00:30:30,340 --> 00:30:31,620
You understand me?

367
00:32:17,900 --> 00:32:19,500
We can stop. We can rest.

368
00:32:19,500 --> 00:32:21,230
We'll rest with the three-eyed raven.

369
00:32:32,410 --> 00:32:33,910
We're not going to make it.

370
00:32:38,780 --> 00:32:40,120
We're already here.

371
00:32:40,120 --> 00:32:40,950
Jojen.

372
00:32:43,450 --> 00:32:44,320
Jojen.

373
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:46,690
Look, Jojen. Look.

374
00:34:08,780 --> 00:34:11,530
Jojen! Come on!

375
00:34:11,530 --> 00:34:13,700
Help them! Now!

376
00:34:14,200 --> 00:34:15,270
Hold on to me!

377
00:34:19,970 --> 00:34:20,780
Hang on!

378
00:34:23,200 --> 00:34:24,610
-Hodor.  -Help them!

379
00:34:24,610 --> 00:34:25,540
Hodor.

380
00:34:26,270 --> 00:34:26,970
Hodor!

381
00:34:48,090 --> 00:34:48,710
Hodor!

382
00:35:09,370 --> 00:35:10,180
Hodor.

383
00:35:13,210 --> 00:35:13,930
Hodor!

384
00:35:45,870 --> 00:35:46,720
Bran!

385
00:35:51,290 --> 00:35:53,150
Save yourself, now!

386
00:36:18,220 --> 00:36:20,120
Come with me, Brandon Stark.

387
00:36:27,760 --> 00:36:28,840
He is lost.

388
00:36:29,630 --> 00:36:31,920
Come with me or die with him.

389
00:36:33,020 --> 00:36:34,180
Go with them.

390
00:37:37,690 --> 00:37:39,200
They cannot follow us.

391
00:37:39,460 --> 00:37:41,880
The power that moves them is powerless here.

392
00:37:43,550 --> 00:37:44,490
Who are you?

393
00:37:44,490 --> 00:37:46,630
The First Men called us the children,

394
00:37:46,740 --> 00:37:48,880
but we were born long before them.

395
00:37:50,040 --> 00:37:51,900
Come, he waits for you.

396
00:39:17,100 --> 00:39:18,620
You're the three-eyed raven?

397
00:39:23,310 --> 00:39:25,000
I've been many things.

398
00:39:26,140 --> 00:39:29,130
Now I am what you see.

399
00:39:31,110 --> 00:39:34,380
My brother, he led us to you and now he.

400
00:39:34,380 --> 00:39:35,830
He knew what would happen.

401
00:39:37,220 --> 00:39:39,320
From the moment he left,

402
00:39:39,380 --> 00:39:42,640
he knew and he went anyway.

403
00:39:42,710 --> 00:39:43,920
How do you know?

404
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:45,440
I've been watching you.

405
00:39:46,540 --> 00:39:47,590
All of you.

406
00:39:48,420 --> 00:39:50,140
All of your lives.

407
00:39:50,670 --> 00:39:53,460
With 1,000 eyes and one.

408
00:39:55,260 --> 00:39:57,760
Now you've come to me at last,

409
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:59,580
Brandon Stark.

410
00:40:00,870 --> 00:40:02,890
Though the hour is late.

411
00:40:03,750 --> 00:40:05,830
I didn't want anyone to die for me.

412
00:40:05,830 --> 00:40:09,460
He died so you could find what you have lost.

413
00:40:11,180 --> 00:40:12,900
You're going to help me walk again?

414
00:40:14,410 --> 00:40:16,180
You will never walk again.

415
00:40:19,240 --> 00:40:20,860
But you will fly.

416
00:40:37,340 --> 00:40:38,360
Podrick.

417
00:40:39,750 --> 00:40:40,780
Podrick.

418
00:40:41,960 --> 00:40:43,350
Where are the horses?

419
00:40:44,770 --> 00:40:46,190
I hobbled them last night.

420
00:40:46,820 --> 00:40:48,150
What sort of hobble?

421
00:40:48,390 --> 00:40:50,110
A figure eight like you taught me.

422
00:40:51,030 --> 00:40:52,460
If you did it like I taught you,

423
00:40:52,460 --> 00:40:53,810
then the horses would be here.

424
00:40:53,810 --> 00:40:54,870
Thieves, maybe?

425
00:40:55,410 --> 00:40:57,650
It's at least 30 miles to the Eyrie from here.

426
00:40:58,630 --> 00:41:00,270
You're carrying the saddlebags.

427
00:41:28,740 --> 00:41:29,850
People coming.

428
00:41:32,070 --> 00:41:34,210
You can shit later. There's people coming.

429
00:41:37,270 --> 00:41:38,240
Morning.

430
00:41:40,460 --> 00:41:41,390
Morning.

431
00:41:43,480 --> 00:41:44,770
I like your sword.

432
00:41:46,240 --> 00:41:48,200
Are we getting close to the Bloody Gate?

433
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:50,860
About 10 more miles.

434
00:41:51,020 --> 00:41:52,240
Did you hear that, Podrick?

435
00:41:52,660 --> 00:41:54,800
Only 10 more miles to the Bloody Gate.

436
00:41:57,200 --> 00:41:58,400
Are you a knight?

437
00:41:58,990 --> 00:41:59,850
No.

438
00:42:00,640 --> 00:42:02,220
But you know how to use that sword?

439
00:42:03,170 --> 00:42:04,220
I do.

440
00:42:05,980 --> 00:42:07,210
Does it have a name?

441
00:42:07,980 --> 00:42:09,160
Oathkeeper.

442
00:42:09,320 --> 00:42:10,570
Mine's Needle.

443
00:42:12,080 --> 00:42:13,090
Good name.

444
00:42:15,590 --> 00:42:17,040
Who taught you how to fight?

445
00:42:18,730 --> 00:42:19,990
My father.

446
00:42:21,900 --> 00:42:23,360
Mine never wanted to.

447
00:42:24,850 --> 00:42:27,070
Said fighting was for boys.

448
00:42:27,380 --> 00:42:28,760
Mine said the same.

449
00:42:29,950 --> 00:42:31,870
But I kept fighting the boys anyway.

450
00:42:32,440 --> 00:42:33,640
Kept losing.

451
00:42:33,780 --> 00:42:36,300
Finally my father said, "If you're going to do it,

452
00:42:36,300 --> 00:42:37,920
you might as well do it right."

453
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:43,810
Seven blessings.

454
00:42:43,990 --> 00:42:46,180
I'm Brienne of Tarth. This is Podrick Payne.

455
00:42:49,300 --> 00:42:50,540
You want something?

456
00:42:51,200 --> 00:42:53,800
That's Sandor Clegane. The Hound.

457
00:43:05,310 --> 00:43:06,830
You're Arya Stark.

458
00:43:07,600 --> 00:43:09,590
I asked if you wanted something.

459
00:43:10,130 --> 00:43:12,760
I swore to your mother I would bring you home to her.

460
00:43:14,240 --> 00:43:15,130
My mother's dead.

461
00:43:15,230 --> 00:43:16,260
I know.

462
00:43:17,910 --> 00:43:19,950
I wish I could have been there to protect her.

463
00:43:21,480 --> 00:43:22,890
You're not a northerner.

464
00:43:22,990 --> 00:43:25,920
No, but I swore a sacred vow to protect her.

465
00:43:27,400 --> 00:43:28,610
Why didn't you?

466
00:43:32,640 --> 00:43:35,490
She commanded me to bring Jaime Lannister back to King's Landing.

467
00:43:35,490 --> 00:43:37,350
You're paid by the Lannisters.

468
00:43:38,330 --> 00:43:40,130
You're here for the bounty on me.

469
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:42,930
I'm not paid by the Lannisters.

470
00:43:42,930 --> 00:43:43,880
No?

471
00:43:46,270 --> 00:43:47,830
Fancy sword you've got there.

472
00:43:48,650 --> 00:43:49,910
Where'd you get it?

473
00:43:52,400 --> 00:43:55,090
I've been looking at Lannister gold all my life.

474
00:43:56,770 --> 00:43:59,240
Go on, Brienne of fucking Tarth.

475
00:43:59,600 --> 00:44:01,690
Tell me, that's not Lannister gold.

476
00:44:02,910 --> 00:44:05,370
Jaime Lannister gave me this sword.

477
00:44:06,290 --> 00:44:07,900
The Bloody Gate is 10 miles.

478
00:44:07,900 --> 00:44:09,540
I swore to your mother by the old gods.

479
00:44:09,540 --> 00:44:10,920
I don't care what you swore.

480
00:44:10,920 --> 00:44:12,920
-Arya!  -You heard the girl.

481
00:44:12,970 --> 00:44:15,450
-She's not coming with you.  -She is.

482
00:44:17,800 --> 00:44:19,460
You're not a good listener.

483
00:44:20,050 --> 00:44:21,600
That Valyrian steel?

484
00:44:21,970 --> 00:44:23,960
I always wanted some Valyrian steel.

485
00:44:23,960 --> 00:44:26,730
Come with me, Arya. I'll take you to safety.

486
00:44:26,730 --> 00:44:29,210
Safety? Where the fuck's that?

487
00:44:29,290 --> 00:44:31,690
Her aunt in the Eyrie is dead. Her mother's dead.

488
00:44:31,690 --> 00:44:33,810
Her father's dead. Her brother's dead.

489
00:44:33,820 --> 00:44:35,810
Winterfell is a pile of rubble.

490
00:44:35,980 --> 00:44:38,310
There is no safety, you dumb bitch.

491
00:44:39,680 --> 00:44:41,190
You don't know that by now,

492
00:44:41,740 --> 00:44:43,890
you're the wrong one to watch over her.

493
00:44:44,240 --> 00:44:45,740
And that's what you're doing?

494
00:44:46,320 --> 00:44:47,800
Watching over her?

495
00:44:48,860 --> 00:44:50,700
Aye, that's what I'm doing.

496
00:45:59,170 --> 00:46:01,160
I have no wish to kill you, Ser.

497
00:46:14,470 --> 00:46:15,960
I'm not a knight.

498
00:47:33,780 --> 00:47:34,860
Arya!

499
00:47:35,690 --> 00:47:36,980
Arya!

500
00:47:38,710 --> 00:47:40,400
Arya!

501
00:47:42,220 --> 00:47:44,330
-Where is she?  -She was just here.

502
00:47:44,410 --> 00:47:45,650
Why weren't you watching her?

503
00:47:45,650 --> 00:47:47,610
I was watching you. I thought you might need some help.

504
00:47:47,610 --> 00:47:49,640
Which way, Pod? Which way did she go?

505
00:47:49,650 --> 00:47:51,090
I think that way.

506
00:47:51,760 --> 00:47:52,990
Arya!

507
00:47:53,850 --> 00:47:55,130
Arya!

508
00:48:24,510 --> 00:48:25,960
You still here?

509
00:48:36,600 --> 00:48:38,210
Big bitch saved you.

510
00:48:39,510 --> 00:48:40,770
I don't need saving.

511
00:48:40,770 --> 00:48:43,270
No, not you. You're a real killer.

512
00:48:43,550 --> 00:48:45,260
With your water dancing

513
00:48:46,090 --> 00:48:47,440
and your Needle.

514
00:48:49,210 --> 00:48:50,370
You gonna die?

515
00:48:50,880 --> 00:48:53,540
Unless there's a maester hiding behind that rock,

516
00:48:54,610 --> 00:48:55,550
aye,

517
00:48:56,850 --> 00:48:58,010
I'm done.

518
00:49:02,350 --> 00:49:04,310
I'd skin you alive for wine.

519
00:49:06,090 --> 00:49:07,500
Fuck water.

520
00:49:09,580 --> 00:49:11,040
Killed by a woman.

521
00:49:13,680 --> 00:49:15,260
I bet you like that.

522
00:49:17,640 --> 00:49:18,580
Go on,

523
00:49:19,850 --> 00:49:21,230
go after her.

524
00:49:22,330 --> 00:49:23,710
She'll help you.

525
00:49:27,550 --> 00:49:29,010
Going it alone,

526
00:49:29,760 --> 00:49:31,870
you won't last a day out there.

527
00:49:32,870 --> 00:49:34,680
I'll last longer than you.

528
00:49:41,820 --> 00:49:43,970
You remember where the heart is?

529
00:49:51,810 --> 00:49:52,920
Fuck it.

530
00:49:53,100 --> 00:49:54,390
I'm ready.

531
00:49:57,460 --> 00:49:58,700
Go on, girl.

532
00:49:59,680 --> 00:50:01,620
Another name off your list.

533
00:50:02,820 --> 00:50:04,520
You kept promising me.

534
00:50:11,830 --> 00:50:13,810
I cut down your butcher's boy.

535
00:50:14,250 --> 00:50:15,650
The ginger.

536
00:50:17,470 --> 00:50:19,200
He was begging for mercy.

537
00:50:19,790 --> 00:50:22,320
"Please, Ser. Please don't kill me.

538
00:50:22,700 --> 00:50:24,550
Please, please."

539
00:50:26,680 --> 00:50:28,500
Bled all over my horse.

540
00:50:29,320 --> 00:50:31,850
Saddle stunk of butcher's boy for weeks.

541
00:50:34,930 --> 00:50:36,370
And your sister.

542
00:50:37,810 --> 00:50:39,310
Your pretty sister.

543
00:50:40,960 --> 00:50:42,860
I should have taken her.

544
00:50:44,330 --> 00:50:46,350
That night the Blackwater burned.

545
00:50:48,310 --> 00:50:50,330
I should have fucked her bloody.

546
00:50:51,560 --> 00:50:54,160
At least I'd have one happy memory.

547
00:51:04,680 --> 00:51:06,550
Do I have to beg you?

548
00:51:11,460 --> 00:51:12,560
Do it.

549
00:51:18,030 --> 00:51:19,190
Do it.

550
00:51:23,090 --> 00:51:24,220
Do it.

551
00:51:54,660 --> 00:51:56,000
Kill me.

552
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:01,430
Kill me!

553
00:52:04,110 --> 00:52:05,480
Kill me!

554
00:52:08,160 --> 00:52:09,410
Kill me!

555
00:52:19,140 --> 00:52:21,770
Oh, get on with it, you son of a whore.

556
00:52:22,390 --> 00:52:24,510
Is that any way to speak about our mother?

557
00:52:25,190 --> 00:52:26,140
What are you doing?

558
00:52:26,140 --> 00:52:27,420
What do you think I'm doing?

559
00:52:27,420 --> 00:52:29,680
A galley's waiting in the bay bound for the Free Cities.

560
00:52:29,680 --> 00:52:31,150
-Who's helping you?  -Varys.

561
00:52:31,150 --> 00:52:33,310
-Varys?  -You have more friends than you thought.

562
00:52:44,850 --> 00:52:46,950
There's a locked door at the top of the stairs.

563
00:52:47,000 --> 00:52:49,380
Knock on it twice, then twice again.

564
00:52:50,150 --> 00:52:51,590
Varys will open.

565
00:52:52,650 --> 00:52:54,380
I suppose this is good-bye, then.

566
00:53:10,620 --> 00:53:12,070
Farewell, little brother.

567
00:53:13,950 --> 00:53:15,110
Jaime.

568
00:53:17,120 --> 00:53:20,300
Thank you for my life.

569
00:53:23,130 --> 00:53:24,530
Quickly now.

570
00:54:44,280 --> 00:54:45,510
Tywin?

571
00:54:49,020 --> 00:54:50,530
My lion.

572
00:56:09,670 --> 00:56:11,340
I'm sorry.

573
00:56:24,530 --> 00:56:25,970
I'm sorry.

574
00:57:13,310 --> 00:57:14,730
Tyrion.

575
00:57:16,490 --> 00:57:18,360
Put down the crossbow.

576
00:57:21,850 --> 00:57:23,480
Who released you?

577
00:57:25,110 --> 00:57:26,640
Your brother, I expect.

578
00:57:26,650 --> 00:57:28,870
He always had a soft spot for you.

579
00:57:29,750 --> 00:57:32,360
Come, we'll go and talk in my chambers.

580
00:57:36,840 --> 00:57:39,480
This is how you want to speak to me, hmm?

581
00:57:39,830 --> 00:57:42,290
Shaming your father has always given you pleasure.

582
00:57:42,290 --> 00:57:43,960
All my life,

583
00:57:44,180 --> 00:57:46,340
you've wanted me dead.

584
00:57:49,290 --> 00:57:50,630
Yes.

585
00:57:51,120 --> 00:57:52,830
But you refused to die.

586
00:57:52,830 --> 00:57:54,420
I respect that.

587
00:57:55,280 --> 00:57:56,820
Even admire it.

588
00:57:56,820 --> 00:57:58,660
You fight for what's yours.

589
00:57:59,510 --> 00:58:01,250
I'd never let them execute you.

590
00:58:01,250 --> 00:58:02,990
Is that what you fear?

591
00:58:03,010 --> 00:58:05,670
I'll never let Ilyn Payne take your head.

592
00:58:05,670 --> 00:58:07,360
You're a Lannister.

593
00:58:09,950 --> 00:58:11,800
You're my son.

594
00:58:14,470 --> 00:58:16,070
I loved her.

595
00:58:16,440 --> 00:58:17,570
Who?

596
00:58:18,680 --> 00:58:19,970
Shae.

597
00:58:20,580 --> 00:58:22,220
Oh, Tyrion.

598
00:58:23,640 --> 00:58:26,180
-Put down that crossbow.  -I murdered her.

599
00:58:27,850 --> 00:58:30,120
With my own hands.

600
00:58:33,550 --> 00:58:36,700
-It doesn't matter.  -Doesn't matter?

601
00:58:37,020 --> 00:58:38,660
She was a whore.

602
00:58:40,370 --> 00:58:42,890
-Say that word again.  -And what?

603
00:58:42,890 --> 00:58:45,170
You'll kill your own father in the privy?

604
00:58:46,650 --> 00:58:47,920
No.

605
00:58:48,730 --> 00:58:50,190
You're my son.

606
00:58:50,730 --> 00:58:52,390
Now, enough of this nonsense.

607
00:58:52,390 --> 00:58:56,050
I am your son and you sentenced me to die.

608
00:58:56,060 --> 00:58:59,550
You knew I didn't poison Joffrey,

609
00:58:59,690 --> 00:59:02,800
but you sentenced me all the same.

610
00:59:03,120 --> 00:59:04,690
-Why?  -Enough.

611
00:59:05,400 --> 00:59:06,680
We'll go back to my chambers

612
00:59:06,690 --> 00:59:08,110
and speak with some dignity.

613
00:59:08,110 --> 00:59:10,570
I can't go back there. She's in there.

614
00:59:10,570 --> 00:59:12,400
You're afraid of a dead whore?

615
00:59:25,430 --> 00:59:27,050
You shot me.

616
00:59:36,170 --> 00:59:38,140
You're no son of mine.

617
00:59:38,140 --> 00:59:39,510
I am your son.

618
00:59:40,880 --> 00:59:43,470
I have always been your son.

619
00:59:58,370 --> 00:59:59,640
What have you done?

620
01:00:01,670 --> 01:00:02,690
Quickly.

621
01:00:06,560 --> 01:00:09,450
Trust me, my friend. I brought you this far.

622
01:02:04,870 --> 01:02:06,370
I want to see the captain.

623
01:02:06,500 --> 01:02:07,690
You're seeing him.

624
01:02:08,450 --> 01:02:10,740
I want to go north to the Wall.

625
01:02:11,530 --> 01:02:12,650
No, you don't.

626
01:02:13,820 --> 01:02:14,770
I can pay.

627
01:02:14,770 --> 01:02:18,380
There is nothing in the North but ice and war and pirates.

628
01:02:18,380 --> 01:02:21,300
I wouldn't need a cabin. Please.

629
01:02:21,700 --> 01:02:23,150
I could work scrubbing the floors.

630
01:02:23,150 --> 01:02:25,770
I'm not going north, child. I'm going home.

631
01:02:26,220 --> 01:02:29,320
-Where's home?  -The Free City of Braavos.

632
01:02:30,420 --> 01:02:32,060
Wait. I have something else.

633
01:02:32,060 --> 01:02:33,880
More silver won't make a difference.

634
01:02:33,880 --> 01:02:36,970
It's not silver. It's iron.

635
01:02:39,980 --> 01:02:40,870
This.

636
01:02:45,520 --> 01:02:46,260
How did you?

637
01:02:46,260 --> 01:02:47,810
Valar morghulis.

638
01:02:50,570 --> 01:02:52,270
Valar dohaeris.

639
01:02:52,610 --> 01:02:55,240
Of course, you shall have a cabin.

